WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.107
A filtered view creates an interesting question about updates.

00:00:04.107 --> 00:00:07.637
Suppose the view shows only active patients.

00:00:07.637 --> 00:00:13.342
Now imagine we update one of those patients through the view and set active to false.

00:00:13.342 --> 00:00:17.507
Without additional protection, the update may succeed.

00:00:17.507 --> 00:00:23.027
The row then disappears from the view because it no longer satisfies the filter.

00:00:23.027 --> 00:00:29.052
The with check option lets us prevent that kind of update when we want the row to remain valid according to the view's

00:00:29.052 --> 00:00:30.939
own condition.
